  "conclusions": [
    "The primary kernel applies the amplitude-channel (S_A) response. At halo virial and disk densities (rho/rho_T ~ 1e-26..1e-25), the stated suppression operator returns S_A = 1 to machine precision, so the unscreened kernel is the model's own output for this channel; amplitude-channel screening first becomes relevant at stellar-interior densities.",
    "The sigma > 165 km/s boundary is a shear-channel (S_Sigma) datum governing dynamical observables; under the pipeline virial map it corresponds to log M_h = 12.1 at z=0, declining to ~10.7 at z=8. It does not transfer to the inference channel (channel-projection notice, manuscript section 4.1).",
    "Even on the dynamical map, ~87% of the UNCOVER sample lies below the shear boundary; the most massive systems (log M_h > 12.5, including the Red-Monster regime) lie above it, predicting suppressed dynamical-channel anomalies there while the amplitude-channel response remains unsuppressed.",
    "The inference channel's environmental dependence is measured directly (steps 094/138): detected at z <= 8 (Delta_rho = +0.30 full sample, +0.20 at z=6-8) and null at z>8 (Delta_rho = +0.04, p = 0.61) - reported as an open tension."
  ]
